{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>And he said, HaShem, etc.; cause to happen, etc.</b> Eliezer was confident in his master that his prayer would be accepted — he having prayed ״He shall send His angel״ etc. — and he added his own prayer that he himself be worthy of having the matter accomplished through him, for sometimes it may happen that there is an impediment to fulfilling the words of the prayer on the part of the agent. Therefore he prayed to the Elohim of his master that He would cause it to happen before him." "<b>And the reason</b> he needed to follow this procedure was that he was concerned lest the family of Abraham mislead him when they learned that he was commissioned and dispatched to take a daughter of theirs — they might give him a maidservant from the families that were with them in the house and say she was of their seed. Therefore he acted shrewdly and followed this procedure with a clear test, which constitutes miraculous disclosure, one that yields more than what he asked of it. Through this too he would know her with an accurate knowledge that she was of the house of Abraham, for she spoke in accord with her innocence without knowing anything about him — that he sought her — and the opening of her words shone forth in her saying (Genesis 24:24) ״The daughter of Betuel״ etc."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:43:03.482768251Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}